@startuml
title Memento / Token / Snapshot

skinparam legendBackgroundColor #f9f9f9
skinparam legendBorderColor #999999

legend right

**Intent**:
Capture and externalize object state to restore later without breaking encapsulation.

**Motivation**:
Undo/redo editors; checkpoints.

**Applicability**:
Need rollback; audit; snapshot/restore.

**Participants**:
Originator creates/consumes mementos; Caretaker stores them.

**Consequences**:
Pros: Encapsulation preserved; simple undo.
Cons: Memory overhead; serialization complexity.

**Implementation Notes**:
Consider differential mementos; compress; cap history.

**Known Uses**:
Text editors; transactional systems.

**Related Patterns**:
Command (undo), Prototype (copy), Snapshot testing.

endlegend

class Originator {
  -state
  +save() : Memento
  +restore(m: Memento)
}

class Memento <<opaque>> {
  -internalState
}

class Caretaker {
  -history : List<Memento>
  +push(m: Memento)
  +pop() : Memento
}

Caretaker o-- Memento
Originator ..> Memento : create/restore
@enduml